Kit 2.0.0 is usable (2026-11-16; verified on the gc-ai film: QA PASS, 0 fail). It adds the LAUNCH FORMAT for new films and for rebuilding the kit 1.1 films; nothing in kit 1.1 was renamed, and films without the opt-in are gated exactly as before. Read video/README.md "Launch format (kit 2)" (beats, rules, daily workflow) and video/kit/README.md "Launch format (kit 2) in one page" (markup); the reference film is video/films/gc-ai (SPEC.md = the beat table, capture/record.cjs = one long 2x take). Opt in: `data-kit-format="launch"` on the root of index.html (plus `data-kit-run="live|example|cached|mixed"`), one host per beat with `data-kit-beat="hook|what|problem|hero|feature|proof|end"` (hook/hero/feature/proof are footage scenes, what/problem are `data-kit-role="statement"` scenes from kit/components/statement-scene.html, end is kit/blocks/launch-end.html with host id `launchend` and variables built/action/url), and one captions host from 0 s to the end card built from kit/components/launch-captions.html: `.kit-cap.kit-cap3` cues (ONE line, <= 8 words, 68 px, no kicker; on screen >= max(2.5, 0.5 + 0.6 x words) s and <= 7 s), one `.kit-hook` cue from 0 s (<= 7 words), one `.kit-proof` cue (`.kit-stats` with 1-3 `.kit-stat` = `.kit-stat-n` + `.kit-stat-l`, plus one `.kit-hood` line), labels in `.kit-cap-tags`, and `<div class="clip kit-chapters" data-kit-chapters="The problem:0|The review:16.2|...">` (3-4 labels over a thin progress bar). In footage scenes: one `<video>` per shot (`data-media-start` from the take's marks), one `"cut": true` keyframe per shot focusing ONE small tracked component (`"maxZoom": 2`), one `.kit-spot[data-kit-focus]` spotlight per shot (kit/components/spotlight.html). Capture at 2x: `cap.startClip({..., viewport: {width: 1360, height: 765}, deviceScaleFactor: 2, cursor: {scale: 0.75, idleHide: 1200}, clickPause: 450})`; build-footage keeps the 2720x1530 pixels and scales boxes/clicks to the 1920 stage. Music: `node kit/scripts/music-bed.mjs films/<slug>` picks bright-pluck-112-long (94 s) when the film outlasts 60 s. Gate: `node kit/scripts/qa.mjs films/<slug> [--frames --every 3.4 | --video renders/x.mp4]` (launch films: 55-90 s, beats present and ordered, <= 2 feature beats, caption words / one line / reading time, chapters, hero and feature shots at >= 1.5x, no camera move under a caption, run label, bed as long as the film). Scaffold: `node kit/scripts/new-film.mjs <slug> --company "Name"` now writes a launch-format film with a beat-table SPEC.md. Background renders need stdin held open: `tail -f /dev/null | npx hyperframes render ...`.
